on of PerfView or Traceevent.\r\n* TraceEvent continues to run on all .NET supported versions of Linux.\r\n\r\n## What's Changed\r\n* Preserve source and callback when cloning predefined dynamic events by @evschaff in https://github.com/microsoft/perfview/pull/2472\r\n* Validate Serialized String Lengths Before Allocation by @brianrob in https://github.com/microsoft/perfview/pull/2474\r\n* Require Windows 10 or Later and Remove 32-bit Support from PerfView by @brianrob in https://github.com/microsoft/perfview/pull/2475\r\n* Validate Kernel Thread And EventPipe Payload Bounds by @brianrob in https://github.com/microsoft/perfview/pull/2476\r\n* Use Sparse Storage For Deserializer Forward References by @brianrob in https://github.com/microsoft/perfview/pull/2477\r\n* Fix LinuxTracing.Tests Architecture Mismatch by @brianrob in https://github.com/microsoft/perfview/pull/2487\r\n* Run FastSerialization Tests In CI by @brianrob in https://github.com/microsoft/perfview/pull/2490\r\n* Enable SHA256 Source Checksums by @brianrob in https://github.com/microsoft/perfview/pull/2491\r\n* ClrMD version bump by @leculver in https://github.com/microsoft/perfview/pull/2478\r\n\r\n\r\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/microsoft/perfview/compare/v3.2.8...v4.0.0","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/perfview/releases/413088983/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":2,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"mentions_count":3}